cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AlleleIQ, please cite it as below."
title: "AlleleIQ: population-inclusive evidence aggregation for clinical genomic variant interpretation"
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Osaro"
    given-names: "Nosakhare Odionfo"
    email: "osaronosakhare@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9778-1161"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NosakhareOsaro/alleleiq"
abstract: >-
  AlleleIQ aggregates evidence for clinical genomic variant interpretation
  and applies ACMG/AMP and ACGS 2024 criteria in a structured, auditable
  way, with explicit reporting of where evidence is thin or absent. It does
  not classify variants: classification remains with a qualified Clinical
  Genetic Scientist. The project's focus is population inclusivity in the
  evidence base underlying interpretation.
keywords:
  - clinical genomics
  - variant interpretation
  - ACMG/AMP
  - ACGS 2024
  - population genetics
  - health equity
  - bioinformatics
